planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- sh record_commit_rpc (moe-agent.sh ~5041-5146) always reads $ATTR_DIR/skipped (non-EXCLUDED, plus the drops file) and $ATTR_DIR/contested, whatever the outcome. ps1 builds each send by hand:
  - the committed $recArgs (~4931) has both lists;
  - the no-candidate send (~4711) has only skipped;
  - the unchanged-tree send (~4819) has neither.
- The daemon (packages/moe-daemon/src/tools/recordCommit.ts):
  - readRecordList THROWS INVALID_INPUT on a non-array skipped or contested;
  - heldContestedPaths reads the held paths from the skip codes. MOE_ATTR_CONTESTED_UNTOUCHED(task-x) carries its peer; strict MOE_ATTR_CONTESTED takes its peer from `contested`, else it names '?';
  - the #governors alert fires when held.length > 0, even for outcome 'nothing'.
- Fake proxy: record_commit appends args to .moe/record_commit.jsonl. Scenario AG reads the LAST row.
- moe-agent.ps1 and postflight.ps1 are UTF-8 with BOM and LF. postflight.sh and moe-agent.sh are LF.

completionSummary:
ps1 nothing landings now send skipped/contested like sh's record_commit_rpc.

- scripts/moe-agent.ps1: new Get-MoeRecordHeldFields($Attr,$Dropped,$Rel) is the single source of the two lists:
  - skipped = non-EXCLUDED skips plus staging drops, first 100;
  - contested = first 100;
  - nulls filtered, paths root-relative, always JSON arrays.
- It is merged with hashtable `+` into three sends:
  - the no-candidate nothing/refused send (Dropped @(); adds the missing contested, so a strict MOE_ATTR_CONTESTED hold names its real peer, not '?');
  - the unchanged-tree MOE_COMMIT_NOTHING_TO_COMMIT send (it had neither list);
  - the committed $recArgs (same lists as before, except contested is now capped at 100 like sh).
- scripts/moe-agent.sh: the nothing record_commit_rpc gets "${LAND_DROPPED_FILE:-}", so an unchanged-tree nothing row carries its drops as on ps1. The no-candidate row is byte-identical to before.

